Here is the complete guide on where and how to deploy your Frontend (React + Vite), Backend (Node.js + Express), and MySQL Database.

🏆 Recommended Deployment Platforms (Best & Free / Low-Cost Options)
Component	Recommended Platform	Alternative	Cost
Frontend (React/Vite)	Vercel or Netlify	Cloudflare Pages / Render	100% Free
Backend (Node.js/Express)	Render or Railway	Fly.io / AWS EC2	Free / Cheap
MySQL Database	Aiven or Railway	PlanetScale / TiDB Cloud	Free Tier Available
🚀 Step-by-Step Deployment Guide
Option 1: The All-in-One Easiest Setup (Railway or Render)
Step 1: Deploy MySQL Database
Aiven (Free MySQL) or Railway:
Go to aiven.io or railway.app.
Create a free account and click New Project → MySQL Database.
Copy the database connection details:
DB_HOST
DB_PORT (e.g., 3306 or provided port)
DB_USER
DB_PASSWORD
DB_NAME
Step 2: Deploy Backend (Render or Railway)
Push your project to GitHub.
Go to render.com (or railway.app).
Click New + → Web Service → Connect your GitHub repository.
Set the configuration:
Root Directory: backend
Build Command: npm install
Start Command: npm start
Add Environment Variables in the dashboard:
env
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5000
DB_HOST=your-mysql-host.aivencloud.com
DB_PORT=your-mysql-port
DB_USER=your-mysql-username
DB_PASSWORD=your-mysql-password
DB_NAME=qrparky_db
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend.vercel.app
Click Deploy. Render/Railway will give you a backend URL like https://qr-parky-api.onrender.com.
Step 3: Deploy Frontend (Vercel)
Go to vercel.com.
Click Add New Project → Import your GitHub repository.
Configure the build settings:
Root Directory: frontend
Framework Preset: Vite
Build Command: npm run build
Output Directory: dist
Add Environment Variable:
env
VITE_API_URL=https://qr-parky-api.onrender.com/api
Click Deploy. Vercel will give you a live URL like https://qrparky.vercel.app.
Option 2: Single VPS Deployment (DigitalOcean / AWS / Hostinger)
If you prefer everything on a single server (Virtual Private Server):

Platform: DigitalOcean Droplet ($4–$6/month), Hostinger VPS, or AWS EC2.
Setup:
Install Ubuntu, Node.js, MySQL Server, and Nginx.
Build frontend: npm run build and serve via Nginx.
Run backend: pm2 start src/server.js.
Setup SSL with free Certbot (Let's Encrypt).
💡 Recommendation:
For fastest deployment with zero server maintenance, go with:

Database: Aiven.io (Free managed MySQL)
Backend: Render.com (Free Node.js web service)
Frontend: Vercel.com (Free fast CDN hosting)